{"availability":"available","full":"jprioses/connect-four-game","name":"connect-four-game","description":"Connect four game made with React","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":4,"forks":7,"created":"2023-03-22T18:30:44Z","updated":"2023-03-28T17:19:05Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jprioses-connect-four.netlify.app/","topics":["figma","framer-motion","netlify","react","react-hooks","react-router"],"demo":"https://jprioses-connect-four.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T04:07:53.452Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T04:07:53.452Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T04:07:53.452Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T04:07:53.452Z","stars":4,"forks":7}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["It's a straightforward game - you just choose how you want to play and start playing. If you choose to play with the CPU, you will always be playing as the red team. Each player has 30 seconds to make a move; otherwise, the other player wins. Every disk you place will drop to the lowest part of the grid column. The one who place 4 disk in row no matter if horizontally, vertically or diagonally.","This project is tagged as advanced in Frontend Mentor and is intended for premium users, so I couldn't see the complete challenge. However, I decided to make it with the tools I had. I did this project to prove my logic, knowledge, and my problem-solving approach at that moment.","In this project, I needed to create an app that allowed users to play with another person or with the machine. So, I decided to first make it for two people and then add some logic for the machine to play as the second player by joining it with the first logic."],"features":["Built With / Hecho con","Development / Desarrollo","Acknowledgements / Agradecimientos"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jprioses/connect-four-game/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e64d9cf49ce0b3121f1947e154959dfabf5213d21b68bf5796355b2b5d6a